---
/** Method: register, joins, cost formula, tests and limits. Every figure comes from the register or params-2026.json. */
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { srcLink } from '../../lib/helpers';
import { breadcrumbSchema, webPageSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
import { displayDate, formatMoney, formatNumber } from '../../lib/format';
import { CITY_INDEX, READ, fareCost, city } from '../../lib/engine/parking';
import P from '../../data/params-2026.json';
const lang = 'en';
const path = route('method', lang);
const title = 'Parkeertabel method 2026: register, formula, tests, limits';
const description = 'How Parkeertabel works out Dutch parking costs in 2026: the National Parking Register tables it joins, the fare formula, tests, known gaps and updates by hand.';
const s = (k: string, t: string) => srcLink(k, lang, t);
const zones = CITY_INDEX.cities.reduce((a, c) => a + c.zones, 0);
const utr = city('utrecht');
const tar01 = fareCost(utr.f['TAR01'] ?? [], 60);
---
<PageLayout title={title} description={description} lang={lang} jsonLd={[webPageSchema({ name: 'Method', description, path, lang }), breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'Method', path }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Method' }]}>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>The Parkeertabel method: how parking costs are calculated</h1>
    <div class="not-prose text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-navy-500">Independent site: not a municipality and not a parking app</div>
    <p>The Parkeertabel method rests on one public source for rates and hours: the National Parking Register (Nationaal Parkeer Register, NPR), which municipalities fill in and the RDW publishes as Open Data Parkeren under a CC0 licence. We downloaded the tables on {displayDate(P.retrieved_at, lang)}; the register itself was last updated on {displayDate(READ, lang)}. The site covers {formatNumber(CITY_INDEX.cities.length, 0, lang)} cities and {formatNumber(zones, 0, lang)} street zones.</p>
    <h2>Four tables joined</h2>
    <p>An area from <Fragment set:html={s('npr_gebied', 'the GEBIED table')} /> is linked to its regulation in <Fragment set:html={s('npr_regeling', 'REGELING')} />, the regulation to its time frames by weekday in <Fragment set:html={s('npr_tijdvak', 'TIJDVAK')} />, and each time frame to a fare made of parts in <Fragment set:html={s('npr_tarief', 'TARIEFDEEL')} />. Only rows valid on the reading date are kept. A zone with no current fare above zero is left out rather than guessed.</p>
    <h2>The cost formula</h2>
    <p>Each fare part covers a span of minutes and charges an amount per step: the cost of a stay is the sum, over the parts, of the steps started times their amount. Utrecht's TAR01 fare, for example, charges per minute and comes to {formatMoney(tar01, 2, lang)} for an hour. A stay that runs across several paid periods, or past midnight, is priced period by period, as a new session in a parking app would be. Free minutes cost nothing.</p>
    <h2>Address to zone</h2>
    <p>The address search sends what you type to the <Fragment set:html={s('pdok', 'PDOK Locatieserver')} /> of the Dutch Cadastre, which returns the municipality and coordinates. The zone is then found in your browser on the area outlines of the <Fragment set:html={s('npr_geo', 'GEOMETRIE GEBIED table')} />. Some municipalities, such as Utrecht and Maastricht, supply no outlines: there you pick the zone from the list.</p>
    <h2>Permits and penalties</h2>
    <p>Resident permits and penalty costs are not in the register. We read them in each municipality's 2026 parking tax by-law on the official local legislation site, for example <Fragment set:html={s('vo_rotterdam', "Rotterdam's")} /> and <Fragment set:html={s('vo_utrecht', "Utrecht's")} />. An automated test finds every amount word for word in the downloaded text. For Amsterdam, The Hague and Delft we found no current by-law in that database and show no figure.</p>
    <h2>Tests and limits</h2>
    <p>Automated tests check the formula on fares from the register (Utrecht per minute, Amsterdam's day ticket, Rotterdam's evening hours), the join for the three largest cities and the by-law amounts. Not covered: private garages outside the register, parking app fees, blue zones, permit-holder bays and event rates. There is no automatic update: we reload the register by hand. Errors can be reported through the <a href={route('contact', lang)}>contact page</a>; how we correct is in the <a href={route('editorial', lang)}>editorial policy</a>.</p>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
